<title>MEXICO: Mexico Senate approves pension plan delay - reports.</title>
<headline>Mexico Senate approves pension plan delay - reports.</headline>
<dateline>MEXICO CITY 1996-11-08</dateline>
<text>
<p>Mexico's Senate late on Thursday approved a six-month delay in the start up date of the private pension funds known as AFORES, various media reports said on Friday.</p>
<p>The private pension funds were scheduled to come into force on January 1, 1997, but will be delayed for six months in order for the government to modify its laws to conform with the new plan.</p>
<p>A majority of the the Senate, or upper house, voted to delay the start up date, said Mexico City newspaper Reforma.</p>
<p>The Chamber of Deputies has already approved the delay, reports said.</p>
<p>-- Mexico City newsroom (525) 728 9559</p>
